  "notes": "Column used: 'Current Maximum Payment' (single rate, population 'all'). Values in the XLSX carry extra decimals (e.g. D2740 816.55119); rounded to cents, matching the PDF version ($816.55). Document is titled 'Effective 1/1/2025' but every requested code shows per-code 'Effective Date' 01/01/2024 (the January 2024 Ohio dental fee increase; 'Previous Maximum Payment' column holds the pre-2024 fees). The ODM page (Dental Services section) says this table 'lists the current fees' and reflects OAC rule 5160-5-01; it is still the only dental table posted as of 2026-10-20, no 2026 edition found. Legend: NC = no coverage, PA = payment determined by prior authorization, BR = by report, D = discontinued. Requested codes not listed at all: crowns D2750/D2790, D2962, D3346-D3348, D4355, D5820/D5821, implants, fixed bridge codes, D7953, D8070, D8090. Age limits/frequencies are in the OAC 5160-5-01 appendix (not reproduced). Most Ohio Medicaid members are in managed care; this is the FFS schedule.",
